WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.250
Hi, I'm Kindle!

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.772
Pele is a new renderer for Mermaid diagrams, built for Obsidian.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:08.333
Here is how it draws them so fast.

00:00:09.892 --> 00:00:13.394
The idea: parse the text, lay out the graph in plain arrays,

00:00:13.394 --> 00:00:16.604
and write the picture as one string, never touching the page.

00:00:18.842 --> 00:00:20.855
A hand-written parser reads the text.

00:00:20.855 --> 00:00:23.204
It is fuzzed against Mermaid's own grammar.

00:00:23.624 --> 00:00:27.074
Labels are measured on a canvas, not on the page, and the

00:00:27.074 --> 00:00:28.799
layout runs over flat typed arrays.

00:00:29.219 --> 00:00:32.240
Then the positions are written straight into one SVG string.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.856
Colours are CSS variables, so a theme change needs no re-render at all.

00:00:38.692 --> 00:00:42.028
The layout is the classic layered recipe, written from scratch.

00:00:42.448 --> 00:00:44.175
Reverse the edges that close a loop.

00:00:44.712 --> 00:00:46.808
Give every node a level, top to bottom.

00:00:47.228 --> 00:00:50.444
Sweep up and down, reordering each level to cut crossings.

00:00:50.864 --> 00:00:53.810
Then assign coordinates, and route the edges so they stay apart.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:59.067
Mermaid measures text by putting nodes in the page, and it copies

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.693
its whole config every time it reads a setting.

00:01:02.113 --> 00:01:05.619
Pele measures on a canvas, has no config to copy, and escapes

00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:06.788
text as it writes.

00:01:08.592 --> 00:01:09.590
I profiled Mermaid.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.583
The biggest cost is not layout or the page.

00:01:12.583 --> 00:01:16.574
It is copying the configuration object, over a third of every render.

00:01:17.967 --> 00:01:21.654
On the same diagrams, Pele was about a hundred to two hundred

00:01:21.654 --> 00:01:25.341
and fifty times faster by median, with a bundle six times smaller.

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:29.423
The speed comes from doing less on every render.

00:01:29.423 --> 00:01:32.965
No page to measure, no config to copy, and one string out.

00:01:34.317 --> 00:01:38.060
Parsers checked against Mermaid, a layout in plain arrays, and a

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.421
string themed by CSS.

00:01:39.841 --> 00:01:41.943
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:41.943 --> 00:01:42.543
I'm Kindle.

00:01:42.543 --> 00:01:42.844
Bye!
